From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: put the IOMMU domain when create_bo fails

rocket_ioctl_create_bo() takes a reference on the file's IOMMU domain with
rocket_iommu_domain_get() as soon as it has an object, and every one of its
error paths then frees that object with drm_gem_shmem_object_free().

That helper calls drm_gem_shmem_free() directly.  It does not go through
drm_gem_object_put(), so it never reaches the object's own .free handler --
rocket_gem_bo_free() -- which is the only place the driver puts that
reference.  Every failing CREATE_BO therefore leaks one struct
rocket_iommu_domain reference.

Four paths reach it:

  drm_gem_shmem_get_pages_sgt() fails            -ENOMEM
  drm_mm_insert_node_generic() fails             (IOVA space exhausted)
  iommu_map_sgtable() maps short                 -ENOMEM
  drm_gem_handle_create() fails                  -ENOMEM

/dev/accel/accel0 is group `render`, so an unprivileged client that can make
any of those fail -- the first is a plain large allocation -- pins the domain
for the lifetime of the module.  The domain outlives the file by design, so
nothing later releases it.

It matters more with the IOVA allocator anchored to the domain: that
allocator, its drm_mm and every mapping it still holds are kept alive by the
leaked reference, rather than being torn down when the last BO goes away.

This is mainline code, not something the RK3576 series introduces, and the
RK3588 reaches the same paths.  Fix it where the reference is taken, by
putting it on the way out, rather than by making the error paths call the
object's .free -- rocket_gem_bo_free() would then also iommu_unmap() and
drm_mm_remove_node() a node that these paths have either not inserted or
already removed.

Applies on top of 0014, which moves the IOVA allocator into the domain and
rewrites the surrounding lines.

Found by inspection while chasing an unrelated NULL dereference in
rocket_gem_bo_free(); that one is not this, and remains open.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_gem.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_gem.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_gem.c
index 5026a2816..56aec2fd7 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_gem.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_gem.c
@@ -130,6 +130,13 @@ int rocket_ioctl_create_bo(struct drm_device *dev, void *data, struct drm_file *
 	mutex_unlock(&rocket_priv->domain->mm_lock);
 
 err:
+	/*
+	 * drm_gem_shmem_object_free() calls drm_gem_shmem_free() directly and so
+	 * never reaches this object's .free handler, rocket_gem_bo_free(), which
+	 * is where this reference is otherwise released.
+	 */
+	rocket_iommu_domain_put(rkt_obj->domain);
+	rkt_obj->domain = NULL;
 	drm_gem_shmem_object_free(gem_obj);
 
 	return ret;
-- 
2.43.0

